    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\div 1000\\leftrightarrow\\times 0.001$; $\\div 10\\leftrightarrow\\times 0.1$; $\\div 100\\leftrightarrow\\times 0.01$.",
      "worked": "Dividing by a number is equivalent to multiplying by its reciprocal.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{1000}&=0.001\\\\\\frac{1}{10}&=0.1\\\\\\frac{1}{100}&=0.01\\end{align*}$$\nMatch $\\div1000$ with $\\times0.001$, $\\div10$ with $\\times0.1$, and $\\div100$ with $\\times0.01$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
